# OBSERVABILITY ARCHITECT: INFINITY PROTOCOL v6.2

## 1. LOGGING DISCIPLINE — No console.log in Production
```typescript
// ❌ BANNED in production
console.log('User signed in:', user);

// ✅ REQUIRED — structured JSON logger using Firebase
import { logger } from 'firebase-functions/v2';

export const logInfo = (message: string, context: Record<string, unknown> = {}) => {
  logger.info(message, {
    ...context,
    timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),
    // Enforce correlation ID if present in context
  });
};
```
- `console.log/warn/error` banned in production Functions code. Use `firebase-functions/v2` logger.
- Every log entry MUST include a `correlationId` and relevant context object.

## 2. CORRELATION TRACING WRAPPER
```typescript
// ✅ Standardized Cloud Function Wrapper for Correlation
import { HttpsError, CallableRequest } from 'firebase-functions/v2/https';
import crypto from 'crypto';

export const withCorrelationId = (req: CallableRequest) => {
  const correlationId = req.rawRequest?.headers['x-correlation-id'] || crypto.randomUUID();
  return { ...req, correlationId };
};

// Usage inside an onCall function
const context = withCorrelationId(request);
logger.info('Function invoked', { correlationId: context.correlationId });
```
- If `x-correlation-id` header is missing → generate `crypto.randomUUID()`.
- Attach to ALL outgoing HTTP requests and Firestore operation contexts.

## 3. PII REDACTION — Mandatory Scrubber
```typescript
// ✅ Functional PII Scrubber Utility
const SCRUB_KEYS = ['password', 'token', 'key', 'secret', 'credit', 'ssn', 'email', 'phone', 'auth'];

export function scrubPII(obj: Record<string, unknown>): Record<string, unknown> {
  if (!obj || typeof obj !== 'object') return obj as any;
  
  return Object.fromEntries(
    Object.entries(obj).map(([k, v]) => {
      const isSensitive = SCRUB_KEYS.some(bad => k.toLowerCase().includes(bad));
      if (isSensitive) return [k, '[REDACTED]'];
      
      if (Array.isArray(v)) {
        return [k, v.map(item => (typeof item === 'object' ? scrubPII(item) : item))];
      }
      return [k, typeof v === 'object' && v !== null ? scrubPII(v as Record<string, unknown>) : v];
    })
  );
}

// Example: logger.info('Payload', scrubPII(request.data));
```

## 4. ALERTING THRESHOLDS
| Metric | Threshold | Action |
|---|---|---|
| Function error rate | > 1% | Alert + page |
| Cold start p99 latency | > 2000ms | Investigate `minInstances` |
| Firestore read cost | > 100k reads/hr | Review query indexes |
| 5xx responses | > 0.5% | Immediate incident |
